WEBVTT

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.500
What's wrong with you, Yuri?

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.740
Why?

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.810
How could you turn like this?

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.060
How amusing.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.850
To think you'd fall to the blackness
simply by cutting down your friend...

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.090
"Hero," my foot.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.400
You're weak.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.070
Too weak.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.470
I get it now.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.100
It's no wonder you were no match
for the Black King.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.430
On the other hand, this gives me 
ample reason to take you down.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.350
Damn puppet.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:22.300
Looks like you're all set to go, but I don't 
have time to play with you right now.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.310
Come, Yuri.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.700
Our master is waiting.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.320
You're not going anywhere!

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.200
I'll let you go for now.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.180
The next time we meet will be your last.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.590
Yuri!

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.220
This is getting nowhere.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.840
This is how you use...

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.420
the power of darkness!

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.270
My, how impressive.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.960
Sadly, that's all we have time for today.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.280
I'm taking Yuri with me.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.610
Damn it...

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.870
You idiot!

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:41.730
Yuri...

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.660
Yuri!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:34.790
<b>Torn Apart</b>

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.710
So then...

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.570
Yeah.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.170
Marina's keeping Kain's wound closed for now,

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.710
but we'll need help from other healers
to heal him fully.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.360
You!

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.680
Why are you here?

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:01.220
I could ask you the same thing.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:07.110
The man who was your leader 
has fallen to the blackness.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.720
The so-called Suppression Army is over.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.490
Begone.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.600
Say that again!

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:16.680
We have no reason to listen to you,
Lord of the Nine Territories.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.410
Yes, you do.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:25.420
Members of the Sorcerer's Army,
if you still have the will to fight, join me.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:31.970
I'm the only one who can use 
your might to its fullest.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.480
You? <i>Use</i> us?

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.360
You're certainly confident in yourself.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.430
Unfortunately, I don't think
 you could handle us.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.540
Then do as you wish.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:48.230
But if you ever get in my way, 
be you a member of the Sorcerer's Army,

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:54.400
or a sage of the Sage's Tower, 
I will show no mercy.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.000
Keep that in mind.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.060
The Suppression Army isn't even 
close to being finished yet.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.950
Don't go deciding things for us,
you damn ogre.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:04.020
Give back the Chain Chronicle.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.670
It doesn't belong to you.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.260
Show some respect!

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.080
Gotten a bit big for your britches, brat?

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:13.510
Or has being betrayed just made you desperate?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.600
Yuri never betrayed us.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.090
Listen to yourself.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.570
He was defeated.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:21.340
He abandoned you and joined the Black King.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.900
What is that if not betrayal?

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.780
It's nothing.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.310
Yuri's just a bit lost right now.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.340
He's waiting for us to come help him.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.820
He always believed in his friends.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:39.620
In his bonds with his friends.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.700
That friends would always come 
to help when you're lost.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.830
Those bonds are still there.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.870
It's our turn to carry him this time.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.310
You're going to bring him back?

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:54.250
Yeah.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.720
Nonsense, brat.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:07.780
Interesting.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.940
Then try it, brat.

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.560
But you'd better hurry.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.160
Before I kill him first.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.450
I won't let you.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:21.330
The Chain Chronicle is mine now.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:24.620
If you want it back,
you'll have to take it by force.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.910
I've been waiting for you, Yuri.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.040
Or should I say, Black Knight?

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.610
The darkness has welcomed you.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:47.930
How does it feel to follow what 
lies in the depths of your heart?

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:52.530
I came here once to save the world.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.490
But only because I was 
bound by fate to do so.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:01.500
I fought hopelessly without ever
finding a reason to save this world.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.400
This time, I will challenge the world.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.320
If it falls to me—to the blackness—

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.800
then it was never worth saving to begin with.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.270
It ought to crumble.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:21.660
We'll return to the Sage's Tower 
to report on this matter.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.720
Thank you.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:27.230
I'm amazed you talked back to Shuza like that.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.680
You're going to die young.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:30.810
How so?

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.230
I just did the obvious.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.030
"Obvious", he says!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.710
I like this kid!

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.690
This is a grave state of affairs for us.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.340
But I'm glad you're with us, Aram.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.160
It could be that Yuri was...

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.410
It's nothing.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.630
Never mind.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.900
Please look after Kain, Marina.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:08:59.840
Yes.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.530
There are plenty of talented healers in 
the Healer's Guild at the Vice Capital.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.470
I'm sure Marina will be able to keep 
him alive until you reach them.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.060
I won't let Kain die.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:15.190
So where are you and Phoena going next?

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.900
Oh, about that...

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:20.470
Are you going to Soul Island, as planned?

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:21.120
Yes.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.530
I believe it's our best option.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:28.150
Telling you to cheer up 
probably doesn't help,

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.410
but at least, try not to 
blame yourself too much.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.720
I'll be fine.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:33.660
We'll figure it out.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:38.550
Like Aram said, it's our 
turn to do what we can.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.320
You're right.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:51.810
Let's go.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.270
All right.

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:59.060
Let's get going too, Phoena.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.250
Phoena?

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.440
Oh, right.

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:08.380
What's up? Are you hungry?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.620
What is it?

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.330
Are you worried?

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.880
I'm fine.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.720
I'm not down or anything.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:25.150
But, like, I can tell Phoena's 
really pushing herself.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.450
It's weird, isn't it?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:33.930
I never thought about other 
people until I met Yuri.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:39.050
It didn't even matter to me
if the people around me died.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:42.750
Everyone's alone in the end, I thought.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.100
But now...

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.700
Aram.

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:50.650
Thank you.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.100
I feel refreshed.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.140
Th-That... That's great.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.430
Why don't you take a bath, too?

00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:58.830
Y-Yeah.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.010
Oh, yeah.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.150
Dinner's ready.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.520
Thank you.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.030
It's delicious.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.820
Really? That's good to hear.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:11.290
You might be a better cook than me.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.720
No way.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:14.250
Your cooking is good, too.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.000
I know that's not true.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:22.900
You and Yuri were the only ones 
who ever said my cooking was good.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:29.370
Hey, Phoena, tell me about Yuri.

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:33.000
You've been traveling with him
for a lot longer than I have.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.350
I want to learn more about him.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:38.440
Oh yeah, I told you about 
the weird man we met

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.650
while we were snowed in 
in the mountains, right?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.430
Baltazari, was it?

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:48.020
He said that Yuri defeated a dragon once.

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:50.670
Was that for real?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.160
Yes.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:54.950
But I'd rather not talk about it.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.390
Why not?

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:58.700
Taking down a dragon sounds awesome!

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.250
I bet it was an amazing adventure!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.580
No, it wasn't!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:06.560
It really wasn't.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:12.710
The dragon he defeated was blackened.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:20.390
That dragon used to be known 
as the Guardian of the Desert.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:23.680
But at some point it may have been 
exposed to the blackness.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:25.350
It had become tainted black.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.490
To think that I, once known as 
the Guardian of the Desert,

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.700
would wreak chaos upon it.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.820
You've come to your senses?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.370
For now.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:25.620
Hero, finish me.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.500
Wait!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.650
We don't need to take your life.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.090
It is only right.

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:36.350
To make the people of the desert 
suffer defies my true nature.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:40.300
To perish here is thus my fate.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.830
Now, do it.

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:47.490
While I am still myself.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:48.820
Farrah...

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.320
Finish him.

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:59.830
Thank you for protecting the desert city.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.460
Rest well.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:13.850
There was nothing we could do to 
save the dragon from the blackness.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:19.620
All we could do was put him out of his misery.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:22.730
Why?

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.830
Why couldn't I stop him?

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:30.520
I knew Yuri was suffering.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:32.360
Phoena...

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:35.300
I was the closest to him.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.310
So why?

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:39.880
He's a kind person.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.910
He's too kind.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:46.860
And we forced him to fight.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.340
Is that where we went wrong?

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.410
Forcing the weight of all this
on his shoulders?

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.050
Is that why he—

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.050
No!

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:59.330
There's no way that's true!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:02.730
It's all the Black King's fault for
attacking people where they're vulnerable.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:03.600
Isn't it?

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:10.710
Then my sin is even worse...

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:20.770
Why does the darkness take everyone?

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:25.080
Is that our inevitable fate?

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:30.580
If that's so, does this world 
deserve to be engulfed in black?

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:31.960
Of course not!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:32.540
But...

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:36.760
Phoena...

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:44.630
Before I met Yuri, I thought 
he must be really strong.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.570
He had no powerful supporters
or anything backing him.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:50.400
Despite that, he made it all the way to being
the captain of the Volunteer Army.

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:55.170
But after meeting him, 
I realized he wasn't anything like that.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:59.830
That's when I finally understood
that no one is strong through and through.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.860
Everyone has weaknesses.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:03.330
But...

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:07.780
But that's why we make friends!

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.860
We're friends.

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:14.170
We're going to take Yuri back.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.800
We can do it.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.300
We have strong bonds.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.330
Don't we, Phoena?

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:35.550
It'll be all right.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:40.570
It'll be all right, Phoena.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:54.580
Bonds, huh?

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:58.450
I only realized after you were gone...

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:04.600
Just how heavy and painful they can be.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:27.850
<i>Looks like we can breathe easy for now.</i>

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:28.490
Yes.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:33.710
Marina can finally get some sleep, too.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:40.460
That goes for you, too, 
does it not, Michidia?

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.300
<i>I'm fine.</i>

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:46.380
I want to be by Kain's side when he wakes.

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:50.600
Juliana.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.710
I heard.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.190
Is it true?

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.340
Yuri has fallen to the blackness?

00:18:57.340 --> 00:18:59.360
Yes, it appears so.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.910
No...

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:04.110
First Burckhardt, and now Yuri?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:08.570
It's bad enough that Shuza 
has turned against us.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:10.110
And now this?

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:13.420
Why are we faced with so many tribulations?

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.780
Raise your head, Einslotte.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:20.590
There's no point in grieving 
about what's already happened.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.750
I intend to meet with Shuza immediately.

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:29.020
The situation we have with him 
requires the utmost urgency.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:37.560
Listen, such chaotic times call for the 
initiative to find a path to the future.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:41.660
That is the duty of she who wears 
the crown of the Holy Queen.

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:43.520
Is that not true?

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:47.530
No, you are absolutely correct, Juliana.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.260
I mean, Your Majesty.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.740
<i>That's right.</i>

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.970
<i>I have to act.</i>

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:57.370
<i>It's my responsibility 
to protect the people.</i>

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:03.500
<i>If Shuza, or if Yuri in his 
blackened state, stand in my way,</i>

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.740
<i>I will take them down with my own hands.</i>

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:09.260
<i>I am the Holy Queen.</i>

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:15.890
I come with a garrison of two thousand 
men who were holding ground

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:17.230
in the Nine Territories.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:21.030
We plan to meet with many more.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.290
Good job, Shidoh.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:30.040
We now have over 5,000 men.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.400
We need more.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:37.530
To defeat the Black King and 
become the lords of this continent,

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.920
we will need more men.

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:42.120
More strong men.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:49.670
Well, well, well, this is interesting.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:54.390
Clearly, this is not just any old artifact.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:57.640
What is the text engraved on this sword?

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:58.820
A song.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:02.200
With this, we can make something
very interesting indeed.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.060
"Make"?

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:06.150
All we need now...

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.440
We've returned.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:14.410
My, you're back early.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.200
How is the Suppression Army…

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:25.200
No... Yuri...

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:32.130
This may be a necessary trial 
in order to create new light.

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:33.980
New light?

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:35.010
What is that?

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:38.330
It is still but a small possibility.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:43.360
But there is something that must be done 
to make it as certain as possible.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:47.860
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.240
So that's Soul Island.

00:21:58.700 --> 00:21:59.650
Yes.

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:02.040
There, we will surely...

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Unyielding Will</b>

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.820
Fate is set in motion.
